prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the Sanilac County record runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids February to March came in under 90% of normal in 34 of those years. In 2025, the middle of the grids got 66% of normal in January to February and 77% in September to October. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 195% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 27790 had its driest year in 1963 at 54% of normal.</p>"}
